<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine car output rises 40.6 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Argentine car output rises 40.6 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine car production in June was up 40.6 percent on June last year but down 6.6 percent on May this year at 36,570 units, the industry lobby ADEFA said Thursday.</p>
<p>Car sales totalled 35,774, which was 24.1 percent higher than the same month last year but 4.0 percent lower than May this year.  </p>
<p>June exports reached 16,868 units, a 91.8 percent increase on June last year and just 2.7 percent short of May's record exports of 17,335.</p>
<p>Accumulated figures for the first six months of the year show a 41 percent rise in production on January-June 1996, a 16.7 percent increase in sales and a 94.9 percent increase in exports.</p>
<p>(( - Stephen Brown, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695))</p>
